setWorkflowMetadata
  ├── when the caller does not have the CONFIG_OPERATOR_ROLE
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when workflowId is zero
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__NoZeroWorkflowId
  ├── when workflow name is zero and owner is nonzero
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__MetadataZero
  ├── when workflow owner is zero and name is nonzero
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__MetadataZero
  ├── when name and owner match the currently registered metadata
  │   ├── when re-submitting the same already-registered identity
  │   │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__MetadataUnchanged
  │   ├── when removing a workflow that is already unregistered
  │   │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__MetadataUnchanged
  │   └── when removing a workflow that was already removed
  │       └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__MetadataUnchanged
  └── when all conditions are met
      ├── it should set the workflow metadata
      ├── it should emit a WorkflowMetadataSet event
      ├── it should increment the workflow's selector-allowlist generation
      ├── when metadata values are zero
      │   ├── it should remove the workflow metadata
      │   ├── it should emit a WorkflowMetadataSet event
      │   └── it should increment the workflow's selector-allowlist generation
      └── when the workflow is already registered and is renamed without going through removal
          └── it should increment the workflow's selector-allowlist generation
